{"tool_name":"pandaseq","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"pandaseq","identifiers":["doi:10.1186/1471-2105-13-31"],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"PANDASEQ is a program to align Illumina reads, optionally with PCR primers embedded in the sequence, and reconstruct an overlapping sequence.","home_url":"https://github.com/neufeld/pandaseq","keywords":["Bacteria","Metagenomics","RNA, Bacterial","RNA, Ribosomal, 16S"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":13},"biotools":{"id":"pandaseq","home":"https://github.com/neufeld/pandaseq","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Paired-end Assembler for DNA sequences (PANDAseq) is a program to align Illumina reads, optionally with PCR primers embedded in the sequence, and reconstruct an overlapping sequence.","addition_date":"2021-05-27T08:32:37Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:21:01.024700Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:pandaseq","credit":[{"email":"jneufeld@uwaterloo.ca","name":"Josh D Neufeld","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["API documentation","General"],"url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/pandaseq/pandaseq.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Demultiplexing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3933"},{"term":"Primer removal","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3237"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"},{"term":"Sequence merging","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0232"}]}],"name":"PANDAseq","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/1471-2105-13-31","metadata":{"abstract":"Background: Illumina paired-end reads are used to analyse microbial communities by targeting amplicons of the 16S rRNA gene. Publicly available tools are needed to assemble overlapping paired-end reads while correcting mismatches and uncalled bases; many errors could be corrected to obtain higher sequence yields using quality information.Results: PANDAseq assembles paired-end reads rapidly and with the correction of most errors. Uncertain error corrections come from reads with many low-quality bases identified by upstream processing. Benchmarks were done using real error masks on simulated data, a pure source template, and a pooled template of genomic DNA from known organisms. PANDAseq assembled reads more rapidly and with reduced error incorporation compared to alternative methods.Conclusions: PANDAseq rapidly assembles sequences and scales to billions of paired-end reads. Assembly of control libraries showed a 4-50% increase in the number of assembled sequences over na\u00efve assembly with negligible loss of \"good\" sequence. \u00a9 2012 Masella et al.; licensee BioMed Central Ltd.","authors":[{"name":"Bartram A.K."},{"name":"Brown D.G."},{"name":"Masella A.P."},{"name":"Neufeld J.D."},{"name":"Truszkowski J.M."}],"citationCount":1633,"date":"2012-02-14T00:00:00Z","journal":"BMC Bioinformatics","title":"PANDAseq: Paired-end assembler for illumina sequences"},"pmcid":"PMC3471323","pmid":"22333067","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Metagenomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3174"},{"term":"Probes and primers","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0632"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0196"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"PANDAseq","home":"https://bio.tools/pandaseq","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Paired-end Assembler for DNA sequences (PANDAseq) is a program to align Illumina reads, optionally with PCR primers embedded in the sequence, and reconstruct an overlapping sequence.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:pandaseq/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":true,"registration":false}